On a serious note, this game has quickly risen to my all time favourites. About 300 hours in, and I was hooked. That may seem like a lot, but once you get addicted and realise how much time your blowing into this game per session, that will seem like diddly♥♥♥♥♥♥to you. With incredible class balance, by far and unarguably the most intricate in game economy of any game in existence and extremely unique gameplay, this game has all the reasonable aspects to make it the optimal addictive free to play model. This free to play game is better than a LOT of triple AAA titles on the market. This is partly due to the fact that almost (like 90%) of the game is available without having to pay a single cent for ANYTHING. This is also due to the fact that when I say free to play, I mean free to play. This is not like any free to play mobile games you will find on Google Play or the App Store. Put your IPods down, kids. This game does not require you to pay money to buy special in game power-ups, buy a new life in case you die too many times or FORCE you to pay money once you get to a certain point. It's freeeeeee. You're freeeeeee from the greedy money grabbin' ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥s on the mobile market. Yes! doesn't freedom feel good people? Anyways, this game will most likely appeal to you if you are... a gamer. Yep. Really this game should entertain you if you just like to play games. Team Fortress 2 does a lot right when it comes to allowing the game to appeal to just about everyone. Fan of MOBA's? RTS's? FPS's? RPG's? Yes yes yes. Everyone I goddamn know plays this game.
That should wrap it up. Yep. This is the best multiplayer game I have ever played. Thank you Valve for making my life better. Praise Gabe Newell. Also did you know Gabe Newell's favourite class is Spy? Huh.

